26. Remove Duplicates from Sorted Array
Difficulty: Easy

Description:
Given a sorted integer array nums, remove the duplicates in-place so that each unique element appears only once. Return the number of unique elements, k.

The first k elements of nums should contain the unique elements in their original order.

Test Case:
Input:  nums = [1,1,2]
Output: 2

Modified nums = [1,2,_]


Why?
Original: [1,1,2]
Unique:   [1,2]


There are 2 unique elements, so the answer is 2.

class Solution {
    public int removeDuplicates(int[] nums) {
        int i=0;
        for(int j=1;j<nums.length;j++){
            if(nums[i]!=nums[j]){
                i++;
                nums[i]=nums[j];
                
            }
        }
        
        return i+1;
    }
}
